      "body": "## Overview\n\n`Olmo3ReasoningParser.is_reasoning_end` returns True if a `</think>` appears anywhere in the prompt, even when the generation prompt then opens a new `<think>`. With the real Olmo-3-7B-Think template, a user message that mentions `</think>` is enough.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Structured outputs no longer constrain the reasoning from the first token for such prompts.\n- Streaming no longer marks reasoning as ended up front, which sent the reasoning out as `content`.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pytest tests/reasoning/test_olmo3_reasoning_parser.py tests/tool_parsers/test_olmo3_tool_parser.py`: 40 passed.\n- The new `test_is_reasoning_end_uses_latest_marker` fails 2 of 5 on main and passes with the fix.\n- pre-commit (ruff, mypy, typos) is clean.\n\n## Details\n\nThe scan now walks back and stops at whichever marker comes last, as `BaseThinkingReasoningParser` and `kimi_k3` already do. `<think>` has two tokenizations (`<th ink >` and `Ġ< think >`), so both are matched.\n\nNot a duplicate: #60353 only flushes the streaming hold-back, and #48160 moves this function over unchanged.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
